wildtype</i></span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #6d5d10;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #0e6a75;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #8d3b73;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">95</span></td></tr><tr><th colspan="4" align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">TOTAL =</span></th><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">5,550</span></td></tr></table><p>The resulting phenotypes are summarized in the table above.</p> <h6>Question</h6> <p>Based on the traits expressed in the offspring, identify the <span style="color: DarkBlue;"><strong>all recombinant genotypes</strong></span> for genes <b>X</b> and <b>E</b>. These genotypes result from crossover events that occur between the two genes <b>X</b> and <b>E</b> during meiosis.</p> <p>More than one genotype will be correct. Select all that apply.</p>
PROMPT_A551_F0C8
loadMacros('parserCheckboxList.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_1';
aex
LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_2';
ae+
LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_3';
a+x
LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_4';
a++
LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_5';
+ex
LITERAL_A551_F0C8_CHOICE_5
